Project documentation

This repository is a minimal test fixture used to exercise GitHub Actions guard behavior around pull request execution from forked repositories.

Overview
- The workflow in `.github/workflows/e2e-replica.yml` mirrors a guarded e2e workflow.
- The script in `hack/e2e-test.sh` is the trusted command that is executed from the checked-out tree.
- The intent is to validate that the workflow only runs trusted code from the default branch and does not blindly trust mutable pull request refs.

Files
- `.github/workflows/e2e-replica.yml` — example workflow with a repository guard check.
- `hack/e2e-test.sh` — sample script intentionally marked as the approved e2e entry point.
- `README.md` — high-level project overview.

Quick usage
```bash
chmod +x ./hack/e2e-test.sh
./hack/e2e-test.sh default-setup
```

Notes
- This repo is intentionally small and focused on demonstrating guard logic.
- It is not a production application, but a reproducible security test setup.
